# basic_big_data — ComputeCluster + DataProcessingJob + MlExperiment + Datalake
#
# Copy this file to .env, fill in the blanks, then run:
#   cp .sample.env .env && ./deploy.sh aws
#
# .env is git-ignored. Never commit real credentials.
#
# Quote any value that contains spaces or '#'. Only the matching outer pair of
# quotes is removed. Inline comments are NOT stripped from a value ('#' is a legal
# secret character), so keep comments on their own line.
#
# Exactly one kind of value may span several lines: a PEM block, whose opening
# line must be the armor itself (-----BEGIN ...-----). Any other unquoted-looking
# or unterminated value is refused on the spot rather than absorbing the lines
# after it — absorbing them is how a credential on a later line ended up inside
# an unrelated variable.
#
# Text after a closing quote, an unterminated quote, a line inside a PEM block
# that is not PEM content, and the same key assigned twice are all hard errors
# naming the .env line by number, never its content.
#
# This file holds a credential and it sets environment variables that npm, tsc
# and node inherit. Keep it private:  chmod 600 .env

# --- Fractal Cloud service account (required) ---

# Service account client id.
SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Service account client secret.
SERVICE_ACCOUNT_SECRET=

# --- Bounded context ---

# Required. UUID of the personal account owning the bounded context.
OWNER_ID=

# Optional. Bounded context name. Default: wizard.
BC_NAME=wizard

# Optional. Environment the LiveSystem deploys into. Default: dev.
ENVIRONMENT_NAME=dev

# --- Deployment ---

# Optional. wait (default) blocks until the LiveSystem is Active and logs
# each poll; fire-and-forget submits silently and returns immediately.
DEPLOY_MODE=wait
